# s1-dl-wire (desktop half): a server window's downloads are this PC's core's. server-file-access.ts createServerFiles now takes
# `core` (an operation of this PC's core) and `serverId` (the window's connection id, which names the core's link to the server);
# until these two hot-file edits are applied apps/desktop `tsc -p tsconfig.node.json` fails at ipc.ts (createServerFiles call).

## apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts, installWindowIpc: the registerDesktopIpc(window, connection.client, { ... }) options
Beside `connectionKind: connection.kind,` add:
    serverId: connection.id,

## apps/desktop/src/main/ipc.ts
1. import: `import { createServerFiles, uploadServerBytes } from './server-file-access';` becomes
   `import { createServerFiles, serverCoreInvoke, uploadServerBytes } from './server-file-access';`
2. DesktopIpcDependencies, beside `connectionKind?: ConnectionKind;`:
     /** The window's connection id (a server window's: the id of this PC's link to the server, which its downloads go through). */
     serverId?: string;
3. registerDesktopIpc destructuring: after `connectionKind = 'local',` add `serverId,`.
4. The `server` constant (connectionKind === 'ssh'): createServerFiles({...}) gets two more options, after `invoke: invokeDesktopOperation,`:
          core: serverCoreInvoke(pcCore ?? protocol),
          serverId: serverId ?? '',
   (an ssh window always has its id from index.ts; `pcCore` is this PC's core connection for a server window, `localProtocol` in index.ts.)
   Nothing else in ipc.ts changes: registerServerFileIpc keeps its options (ipc-server-files.ts reads server.downloads).

## Tests that follow the protocol rows (PROTO-WIRE; see pending-rows/s1-dl-wire.rows [inventory])
apps/desktop/src/main/protocol/desktop-operation-route.test.mjs: `operations.length` 166 -> 171 and the five CASES rows listed there. Until the
inventory rows land, 'the routed operations are the spec map targets with params the Rust schema declares' fails (it holds the routed names to the map).

## Not changed here (not mine): shared/server-files.ts keeps SERVER_DOWNLOAD_MAX_BYTES, no TypeScript reader remains (the 2 GiB limit is the core's
SERVER_DOWNLOAD_MAX_BYTES in mixdog-workspace serverdownload.rs); delete the constant with the next edit of that file if no caller appears.
